---
source: crates/gws-rust/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Google Workspace CLI: every Workspace API, built at runtime from Google's Discovery documents

Usage: gwsr [OPTIONS] [COMMAND|SERVICE]

Commands:
  auth         Sign in, inspect and manage credentials (run `gwsr auth --help`)
  schema       Show the request/response schema of a method or type
  commands     Inventory of services, resources, methods and helpers with their flags (JSON; `--format table|csv` gives one row per command)
  completions  Print a shell completion script (dynamic: completes services, resources and methods from cached Discovery documents)
  batch        Send many API calls in multipart/mixed batch requests (NDJSON in, NDJSON out)
  cache        Manage the local Discovery document cache
  help         Show help for a command or service (`gwsr help drive files list`)
  dev          Maintainer tools

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Global options:
      --format <FORMAT>        Output format [default: json, or `format` in config.toml] [possible values: json, table, yaml, yml, csv]
      --jq <EXPR>              Filter output with a jq expression (string results print raw)
      --columns <COLS>         Columns for table/csv output, comma-separated (dot paths for nested fields)
      --compact                Single-line JSON (default when stdout is not a terminal)
      --pretty                 Indented JSON (default on a terminal)
      --dry-run                Validate the request locally and print it without sending it
      --sanitize <TEMPLATE>    Screen API responses through a Model Armor template (projects/P/locations/L/templates/T; env: GWSR_SANITIZE_TEMPLATE)
      --api-version <VERSION>  Override the service's API version (e.g. v2); also `<service>:<version>`
  -v, --verbose...             More diagnostics on stderr (-v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace)
  -q, --quiet                  Only print errors on stderr
      --profile <NAME>         Credential profile (env: GWSR_PROFILE; default: `profile` in config.toml, set by `gwsr auth use`, then "default")
      --impersonate <EMAIL>    Service accounts only: act as this user via domain-wide delegation (env: GWSR_IMPERSONATE)

Services:
  drive              Manage files, folders, and shared drives
  sheets             Read and write spreadsheets
  gmail              Send, read, and manage email
  calendar           Manage calendars and events
  admin-reports      Audit logs and usage reports (also: reports)
  admin              Manage users, groups, org units, devices, and roles (Admin SDK Directory) (also: directory, admin-directory)
  datatransfer       Transfer user data between accounts (Admin SDK Data Transfer) (also: admin-datatransfer)
  alertcenter        Manage Workspace security alerts
  cloudidentity      Manage identity groups, memberships, and devices
  groupssettings     Manage Google Groups settings
  licensing          Assign and manage product licenses
  reseller           Manage reseller customers and subscriptions
  vault              Manage eDiscovery matters, holds, and exports
  driveactivity      Query activity on Drive files and folders
  drivelabels        Manage Drive labels and classification
  chromemanagement   Chrome browser and ChromeOS device reports and telemetry
  chromepolicy       Manage Chrome policies for users and devices
  postmaster         Gmail sender reputation and delivery metrics (Postmaster Tools) (also: gmailpostmastertools)
  cloudsearch        Manage Cloud Search data sources and queries
  docs               Read and write Google Docs
  slides             Read and write presentations
  tasks              Manage task lists and tasks
  people             Manage contacts and profiles
  chat               Manage Chat spaces and messages
  classroom          Manage classes, rosters, and coursework
  forms              Read and write Google Forms
  keep               Manage Google Keep notes
  meet               Manage Google Meet conferences
  events             Subscribe to Google Workspace events
  modelarmor         Filter user-generated content for safety
  workflow           Cross-service productivity workflows (also: wf)
  script             Manage Google Apps Script projects

Usage: gwsr <SERVICE> <RESOURCE> [SUB-RESOURCE] <METHOD> [--params JSON] [--json JSON]
Example: gwsr drive files list --params '{"pageSize": 5}' --format table

Environment:
  GWSR_TOKEN               Pre-obtained OAuth2 access token (highest priority)
  GWSR_CREDENTIALS_FILE    Path to an OAuth or service-account credentials JSON file
  GWSR_CLIENT_ID           OAuth client ID (for gwsr auth login)
  GWSR_CLIENT_SECRET       OAuth client secret (for gwsr auth login)
  GWSR_CONFIG_DIR          Config directory (default: ~/.config/gwsr)
  GWSR_KEYRING_BACKEND     Keyring backend: keyring (default) or file
  GWSR_PROJECT_ID          GCP project for quota and billing
  GWSR_FORMAT              Default output format (json, table, yaml, csv)
  GWSR_JSON_STYLE          JSON layout: auto (default), compact, pretty
  GWSR_PAGE_LIMIT          Default --page-limit
  GWSR_PAGE_DELAY_MS       Default --page-delay
  GWSR_SANITIZE_TEMPLATE   Default Model Armor template (--sanitize)
  GWSR_SANITIZE_MODE       Sanitization mode: warn (default) or block
  GWSR_LOG                 stderr log filter, e.g. gwsr=debug (RUST_LOG is also honored)
  GWSR_LOG_FILE            Directory for JSON log files (daily rotation, mode 0600)
  GWSR_COMPLETE            Set by the shell completion script; do not set manually

Exit codes:
  0    Success
  1    API error      — Google rejected the request (permanent; do not retry unchanged)
  2    Auth error     — credentials missing, expired or invalid
  3    Validation     — bad arguments, flags, config or input
  4    Discovery      — could not fetch or parse the API schema
  5    Internal       — unexpected failure (I/O, serialization, ...)
  6    API retryable  — rate limit (429/403 rateLimitExceeded) or server error (5xx); retry with backoff

Output is JSON by default (compact when piped); --format table|yaml|csv is opt-in.
Errors: one JSON object {"error":{...}} on stderr (human text with a human --format);
stdout stays empty on failure.
Config: ~/.config/gwsr/config.toml (flag > env > config > default).
This is not an officially supported Google product.
